    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Zeebo Deebo is an art game and an undefinable fever dream. An interactive experience of connected and disjointed fragments of Zeebo's mind, that eventually reflect your own choices back to you as you play through the different weird sections.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3754110/extras/3bc83498db9afb1acd12364bc5efe530.poster.avif?t=1749478470\" width=600 height=337 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3754110/extras/3bc83498db9afb1acd12364bc5efe530.webm?t=1749478470\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span><br><br>  Do you know what a collage is? An assembled artwork that mixes anything you like -photographs, paper, fabric, or other objects\u2014onto a surface. That's what Zeebo Deebo is. Only this collage is interactive. It's a mish mash of feelings, scenes, events, for you to live through.\u00a0<br><br>You will get profiled. You will find out for example how many birds you have devoured in your dreams. What this means depends on your IQ, EQ, GQ, as well as your hormone levels. <br><br>You get to control Zeebo in different forms, elements of his mind, and...other things...until it ends. Not much else can be said about it apart from the fact there is quite probably nothing else like it! Enjoy. :)<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3754110/extras/7c7b6c43e28c4290c1e2c6e3f19d1f57.avif?t=1749478470\" width=600 height=435 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FAQ</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <strong>What genre is this game?</strong> <br>Any, but not one and not all.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <strong>Will I be enlightened after this?</strong> <br>You will certainly not be the same.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <strong>Is this a form of therapy?</strong> <br>Apparently 3 out of 10 people say they got traumatized by it.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >THANKS</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game was made possible by Phineas Gage, Srinivasa Ramanujan, John von Neumann, Gabe Newell, Georg Cantor, Salvador Dal\u00ed, David Lynch, Felix the Cat, Lassie,  as well as the Unfairy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
